WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.520
- I'm onto you.
- You should have killed me

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.200
when you had the chance.

3
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.440
I'm drunk on power.

4
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.120
SHE LAUGHS

5
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.240
- There's a "Hug" in my name.
- But get too close.

6
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.960
there'll be a dagger in your back.

7
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.520
22 players arrived at
this Scottish castle.

8
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.800
hoping to win up to £120.000.

9
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.840
This game has
officially started.

10
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:24.880
One by one.
the Faithful have fallen.

11
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.760
"By order of the Traitors.
you have been murdered."

12
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.040
And with two Traitors
caught along the way...

13
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.800
Traitor!

14
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.800
CHEERING

15
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.880
A Traitor.

16
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.880
CHEERING

17
00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.720
..now two Traitors
and four Faithful remain.

18
00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.800
After an uphill battle
in the mission...

19
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.080
Go!

20
00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.440
Come on. we need this!

21
00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.320
..the Faithful were rewarded.

22
00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:52.440
You have stopped the Traitors
committing their final murder!

23
00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.320
At the penultimate Round Table...

24
00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.720
James. last night's behaviour.
I haven't been able to look past it.

25
00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:00.560
..suspicions intensified...

26
00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.640
If you were a Traitor.
the possibility that you saw Fiona

27
00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.000
and was like. "I don't want to work
with this person. Get her out now."

28
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.040
That's one of
my proudest achievements.

29
00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.800
Don't take that away from me.

30
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.680
..but with the votes
reaching deadlock...

31
00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:11.760
I'm sorry. James.

32
00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:16.600
James and Rachel. the banishment
will be decided by chance.

33
00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.280
..who will make it to the final

34
00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:21.560
and be in with a chance
of taking home the prize?

35
00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.920
This is The Traitors Final.

36
00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:43.160
James and Rachel.
this is for a place in the final.

37
00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.920
Whoever's chest contains a Shield.

38
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.680
you are saved from
tonight's banishment.

39
00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:01.800
Please open the chest...

40
00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:04.680
..in three...

41
00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:08.360
..two...

42
00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:11.760
..one.

43
00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:23.960
Hey-ho!

44
00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:29.680
Rachel. you have the Shield.
You are safe from banishment.

45
00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.240
James. your chest did not
contain a Shield.

46
00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:36.120
You have been banished.
Please come up here and join me.

47
00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.480
James. you have been banished
from the castle.

48
00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:50.880
Please reveal. are you a Faithful
or are you a Traitor?

49
00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:55.640
It's been amazing.
I've learned a lot about myself.

50
00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:58.200
And it's just been
an incredible experience.

51
00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.160
I feel strangely serene right now.

52
00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.960
What a game.
Thank you.

53
00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.960
At the first Round Table.
when the blindfolds went on.

54
00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.440
I was selected immediately -
and have been from the start -

55
00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:13.080
as a trait-ful...

56
00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:17.840
..Faithful.

57
00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.040
GROANS

58
00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.560
Good luck. everyone. Good luck.
Been a pleasure.

59
00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:28.240
No. No. no. no. no. no!

60
00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:40.000
Faithful. you have lost
one of your own

61
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:43.760
at such a late stage in the game.

62
00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:48.320
However. the good news.
there is no murder.

63
00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:53.240
Also. you are my finalists.
Congratulations.

64
00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:54.520
Have a wonderful evening.

65
00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:58.760
No.

66
00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:02.440
That was horrible.

67
00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.240
I knew I was going to come
under fire.

68
00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:12.360
but to leave it to chance.
like. that was just unbelievable.

69
00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:19.200
I really. really appreciated
Stephen's support tonight.

70
00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:23.240
He had my back.
So. yeah. it didn't go unnoticed.

71
00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.960
I appreciate you
listening to me. Jack.

72
00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.360
if it doesn't mean much now.

73
00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:44.400
- You all right?
- Yeah.
It was really kind of horrible.

74
00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.840
Yeah. I can't imagine.
Like. the chance stuff is crazy.

75
00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:50.480
- It's really frustrating the way
all this is playing out.
- Mmm.

76
00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:52.040
I was going to enjoy
standing up there and telling you

77
00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:55.240
that I'm a Faithful and kind of
rubbing it in people's faces.

78
00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:57.440
But it just looks so bad that
it was me and him up

79
00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:00.080
and then he says that. cos it's just
going to look directly at me.

80
00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:02.840
And that's the way the whole thing
is constructed.

81
00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:09.080
- It's not just you. Here.
- I shouldn't have changed mine.

82
00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:10.840
He's just been himself
the whole time.

83
00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:13.680
I just... I just wasn't convinced
by what he said.

84
00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:16.920
I've taken James's chance away
of being in the final

85
00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.200
and he was a Faithful.
and I feel terrible.

86
00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.360
Cos he was my mate.

87
00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.480
I shouldn't have changed my mind.

88
00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:31.440
- This is an impossible game.
- It's so hard.

89
00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.360
- It's so hard.
- How are we supposed to know?

90
00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:37.960
I so almost put Rachel's name down
on that final vote.

91
00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:39.640
If we got Rachel out tonight.

92
00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:43.200
knowing how the room was feeling
about me in general.

93
00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:47.800
I think it would have just
been easier for me

94
00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:50.400
to get to the endgame by myself.

95
00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.200
I really underestimated
how difficult this would be.

96
00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:03.480
- All right?
- Yeah.

97
00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:06.400
- Obviously. just shitting it.
- It's awful.

98
00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:07.800
Yeah. I know.

99
00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.520
What you said to me
out there as well

100
00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:14.120
is sort of making me think
I did make a mistake today.

101
00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:17.480
I know you've made a mistake.

102
00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:19.800
This game is so frustrating.

103
00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:21.880
Straight after the Round Table.
I felt as if

104
00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:25.800
the way Rachel came across
did seem really Faithful.

105
00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:28.880
She just said to me she was quite
looking forward to standing up there

106
00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:31.160
and rubbing it in our faces
that she was a Faithful.

107
00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:33.240
I resonate with that
because I'd feel the exact same

108
00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:34.880
if I was to stand up there.

109
00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:38.760
and I feel that leads me
towards Stephen and Jade.

110
00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:42.240
Jack. it mightn't mean an awful lot
now. but I appreciate your vote.

111
00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:48.520
How are you feeling?

112
00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:52.960
Obviously it's just
very carefully manipulated around

113
00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:57.120
to make it look like me. because if
I was a Faithful. I would murder me.

114
00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:02.000
Or if I was a Traitor.
I would murder me.

115
00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.040
Mm-hm.

116
00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:11.160
I almost feel like Jack
is mad at me.

117
00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:13.480
He's disappointed in himself
that he changed his vote.

118
00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:17.000
I get it. You know. I could have
changed my vote to Rachel

119
00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.000
and Rachel could have gone.
and she could have been a Faithful.

120
00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.040
and then I'd still be upset
because I got it wrong again.

121
00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:24.360
- And you just don't know.
- I know.

122
00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:27.000
It's hard to vote for your friend.

123
00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:30.080
I really don't think
Jack is a Traitor.

124
00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:34.400
I think he was genuinely upset
when James was banished.

125
00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.760
It's really difficult.

126
00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:41.320
It was really hard
to re-evaluate my vote.

127
00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:44.000
just because. you know. James
has been a big support for me.

128
00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.880
He's never been suspicious of me.

129
00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:47.480
But in the end of it.

130
00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:51.080
I had to stick with my feelings
and vote for Rachel.

131
00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:53.560
I think there are still two Traitors
left in this game.

132
00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:56.000
and it's going to take everything
that we have to find them.

133
00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:01.320
It's just reminded me
that this is a game.

134
00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:05.920
SHE CHUCKLES

135
00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:05.920
You can't help but laugh.

136
00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:08.920
Like. it is absolutely brilliant.

137
00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:14.240
CLOCK CHIMES

138
00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:23.120
All right. See you later.

139
00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:30.880
The castle clock
has struck midnight.

140
00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:33.080
It's been an eventful evening.

141
00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:35.000
The Faithful are off to bed.

142
00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.000
The Traitors. well. they're off
to the Turret.

143
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:41.440
There isn't a murder. but there's
a lot of planning to be done.

144
00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:46.120
# Soldiers marching on

145
00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:49.600
# Survivors standing strong... #

146
00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:53.560
I really put my neck on the line
to keep Rachel in the game.

147
00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:57.240
And I told myself
from the very beginning.

148
00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:01.080
I had to make it through
this experience as a Traitor

149
00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:04.640
with my moral compass still intact.

150
00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:08.080
But I need to start
putting myself first

151
00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:11.120
and making sure that I have the best
chance of winning this game.

152
00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:15.480
# At the edge of the world

153
00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:17.080
# Soldiers. #

154
00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:21.640
God! I thought it was curtains
for you.

155
00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:23.080
Me too.

156
00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:24.400
That was hard.

157
00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:27.680
But I didn't come here
just to lie down and roll over.

158
00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:30.160
I came here to fight my way
to the final.

159
00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:34.360
And I had luck on my side.
but that's what I've done.

160
00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:37.120
We need to be really. really aligned
tomorrow. Rachel -

161
00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:39.240
- because if not...
- We're done.

162
00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:41.840
- ..neither of us are going to get
to that money.
- No.

163
00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:46.280
I appreciate that you didn't vote
for me.

164
00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:52.440
And we've played as a team the whole
time. and that's helped our game.

165
00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:53.920
Let me tell you now -

166
00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:58.160
if I wanted to take the money. I
would have got rid of you tonight...

167
00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.080
- I know.
- ..because I think
it would have only helped my game.

168
00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:05.120
I'm on the ropes. but I'm not
going down without a fight.

169
00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:11.440
Whatever you think we need to do
tomorrow. I'm very willing to do.

170
00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:13.560
We are this close to the finish line

171
00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:15.680
and I hope he has my back.

172
00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:20.680
And if he doesn't. God help him.
because I would take him down.

173
00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:26.960
- Please trust me.
- I do.
- Please do not turn on me tomorrow.

174
00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:28.280
I have no other play.

175
00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:31.840
so I'm putting every ounce of trust
in you. Stephen.

176
00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:36.360
You know. I'm saying the right
things. but I just don't...

177
00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:39.080
I don't know what to do tomorrow.

178
00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:42.400
# We'll take it all. #

179
00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:45.280
Goodbye. Turret!

180
00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:49.400
# So it begins... #

181
00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:54.680
Movin' On Up
by Primal Scream

182
00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:00.920
# I'm movin' on up now

183
00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:06.480
# Gettin' out of the darkness... #

184
00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:11.400
After ten banishments
and seven murders.

185
00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:15.240
only five players remain
in the game.

186
00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:18.640
and it's time for the finalists
to return to the castle

187
00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:20.960
for their last breakfast.

188
00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:24.000
# My light shines on! #

189
00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:30.480
On my own.

190
00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:34.480
I'm in the final!

191
00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:34.480
SHE LAUGHS

192
00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:36.360
It's the best feeling ever.

193
00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:39.360
It genuinely is the best feeling.

194
00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:41.560
I've got here by the skin
of my teeth.

195
00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:47.400
Oh. my stomach's in knots.
like butterflies!

196
00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:50.200
I was so nervous
when I arrived to the castle.

197
00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:53.360
And I doubted myself and thought.
"I don't know if I can do this."

198
00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:55.480
From the tap on the shoulder
at the start...

199
00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:58.600
You are officially a Traitor.

200
00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:00.640
..I settled and I was loving it.

201
00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:03.640
Rachel is in that confessional.

202
00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:05.840
The whole Harriet
in the confessional box

203
00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:08.000
scared the life out of me.

204
00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:10.240
I thought. "I just want to go home!"

205
00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:11.640
Fiona!

206
00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:12.720
I am not a liar!

207
00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:16.040
Fiona. when you tell a lie.
you're a liar.

208
00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:19.000
You are a Traitor.

209
00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:20.800
I have loved this experience.

210
00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:25.120
And I will do whatever it takes
to get me to that fire pit.

211
00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:31.120
- I will not write your name down.
- I will not write your name down.

212
00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:33.800
It would be absolutely amazing

213
00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:36.960
to win that money for me
and for my mum and the kids.

214
00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:39.640
To be the first female Traitor
to win this game

215
00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:42.840
would be something else. And I want
to take it home for the girls.

216
00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:45.920
KNOCK ON DOOR

217
00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:47.360
Come in!

218
00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:51.560
Hello. hello. hello!

219
00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:52.960
Hello. finalist!

220
00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:54.080
You all right?

221
00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:56.920
I'm buzzing to be in the final.
Never thought I'd make it.

222
00:12:56.920 --> 00:13:00.480
Faraaz. Nice to meet you.

223
00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:03.960
This experience has been
an absolute roller-coaster.

224
00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:05.560
It's taught me a lot about myself.

225
00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:07.400
It's taught me a lot about
meeting people

226
00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:09.000
from all different walks of life.

227
00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.360
- Genuinely. I hope I see yous all
tomorrow. yeah?
- Yeah.

228
00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:13.680
I am proud of the way
that I've played this game.

229
00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:16.720
I think it's good that everyone
understands that it is a game.

230
00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:19.120
I've voiced my opinions
and I've always voiced them

231
00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:20.880
with logic and reason behind it.

232
00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:23.480
- I did feel like you got
quite defensive.
- Yeah. I did.

233
00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:25.720
- I snapped at you and I'm sorry.
- No. no. It's fine. You can do it.

234
00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:26.800
I'm not arsed. truth.

235
00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:28.840
I was nervous at the start
to bring points up...

236
00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:29.880
Could I start. please?

237
00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:31.080
..but once I got that off my chest.

238
00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:34.760
I knew I was capable
of doing anything in this game.

239
00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:37.280
Winning The Traitors
would mean so much.

240
00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:38.480
No way!

241
00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:42.480
I honestly love my mum and dad. and
that money would mean a lot to me

242
00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:45.880
because of the experiences
that it would be able to unlock

243
00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:47.080
for me and my family.

244
00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:48.520
It would be unbelievable.

245
00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:52.200
It's weird that
you don't have to say.

246
00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:53.960
"I wonder who's not going
to come back..."

247
00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:55.960
I know. when you know
everyone's coming.

248
00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:57.840
KNOCK ON DOOR

249
00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:57.840
Come in.

250
00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:04.040
- Hello!
- Hi!
- Good morning.
- Good morning! How are you both?

251
00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:07.240
- Good. How are you?
- Good.
- Good.
- Oh. gosh.

252
00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:09.920
So exciting! I'm in the final.

253
00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:11.360
- My hands are getting sweaty.
- Yeah!

254
00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:14.120
I don't really know
how I'm still here.

255
00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:16.320
Please go into the castle.

256
00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:16.320
CHEERING

257
00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:19.040
From the start.
everyone had their doubts about me.

258
00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:20.920
People have pointed fingers
at the way that I looked

259
00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.520
after the Traitors pick.

260
00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:27.040
- You just looked...scared.
- I cannot control how my body reacts.

261
00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:30.120
My gut instinct is that
you are a Traitor.

262
00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:33.280
For someone to have gone through so
much and. like. defended themselves

263
00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:35.640
every single day at the Round Table.

264
00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:39.560
it kind of then made me start
doubting myself a little bit.

265
00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:41.280
I found a Shield token!

266
00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:44.160
But my self-belief
has definitely developed

267
00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:47.360
and I love the friendships
and the connections I've formed.

268
00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:49.680
You're one of the people
that I'm most proud of in here.

269
00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:51.640
I'm going to start crying.

270
00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:52.840
Don't!

271
00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:54.000
It's been wonderful.

272
00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:55.600
Just the next step is to win.

273
00:14:57.240 --> 00:14:58.600
KNOCK ON DOOR

274
00:14:57.240 --> 00:14:58.600
Come in!

275
00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:05.000
- Good morning!
- Good morning!
- Morning.

276
00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.760
We made it!

277
00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.760
HE LAUGHS

278
00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:10.640
Somebody's very happy.

279
00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:12.600
I can't believe we made it.

280
00:15:12.600 --> 00:15:14.160
Darling...

281
00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:18.280
I can't believe I'm here!

282
00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:23.360
When Claudia tapped my shoulder. my
heart was beating out of my chest.

283
00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:25.520
I feel like the first half
of this experience.

284
00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:26.840
I was an emotional wreck.

285
00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:27.960
Just can't get my head around

286
00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:29.560
how you've come back today.
to be honest.

287
00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:34.080
But I've grown in confidence
and I'm super proud of myself.

288
00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:38.600
I have been embroiled
in many controversies.

289
00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:41.880
- Who do you think the Traitor
in the box is?
- Stephen.

290
00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:44.760
The Caged Nine. The Library Five.

291
00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:51.000
Why are we not looking at
who was in that room?

292
00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:52.400
HE SCREAMS

293
00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:55.080
For the first time.
I really feel like

294
00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:57.600
the odds are stacked in my favour.

295
00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:00.960
- We could take the Celtic connection
right to the end.
- I know!

296
00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:04.360
Rachel and I made a promise
to each other

297
00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:07.560
that we would never write each
other's names down on our slates.

298
00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:12.560
but at this point now. I have
to think of myself as an individual.

299
00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:14.280
It's not an easy decision.

300
00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:17.320
I don't know what to do.

301
00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:22.720
I really hope our last mission
doesn't involve any running.

302
00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:25.400
I won't...
You'll have to carry me across.

303
00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:26.880
Piggyback.

304
00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:26.880
KNOCK ON DOOR

305
00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:28.200
Come in!

306
00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:32.080
Hello!

307
00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:32.080
LAUGHTER

308
00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:34.040
We're in the final!

309
00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:35.080
Hello. everyone!

310
00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:38.760
Oh. my God!
I'm part of the final five.

311
00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:40.840
We're smashing it. guys!

312
00:16:40.840 --> 00:16:43.960
To get to the final
and not have a single vote.

313
00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:45.080
I'm happy with that.

314
00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:49.680
I've just been me.
and I've just been open and honest.

315
00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:53.400
I'm the sort of player
that wears his heart on his sleeve.

316
00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:57.840
And I think that is a big reason as
to why I've got so far in this game.

317
00:16:57.840 --> 00:17:00.720
Reece. I'm just going to
stick with my guts.

318
00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:02.800
Although I've made my fair share
of mistakes...

319
00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:06.000
I was 50-50 between the two of you.

320
00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:07.120
I'm sorry. James.

321
00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:09.040
..I'm not going to
get it wrong tonight.

322
00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:10.600
THEY CHEER

323
00:17:10.600 --> 00:17:13.240
I've got over
that little emotional blip.

324
00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:18.320
And now I see with so much clarity
that Rachel is the Traitor.

325
00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:20.320
I'm just going with my gut.

326
00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:21.960
I have so much belief
that I can do it.

327
00:17:21.960 --> 00:17:25.200
I can carry myself through.
take home the money.

328
00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:26.640
I can't stop believing.

329
00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:29.080
And us Faithfuls.
we're going to be victorious.

330
00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:33.240
- I mean. it's been hard to see
a lot of people go.
- Yeah.

331
00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:34.600
But I think James is my friend

332
00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:37.920
- and I'm doing this for James now
as well.
- Aw!
- Good. good. good.

333
00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:40.440
But we're in the final.
though. How amazing!

334
00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:42.680
- I mean...
- You guys.
you've all done so well.

335
00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:44.000
Likewise.

336
00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:57.080
- Players.
- Good morning!
- Good morning. finalists!

337
00:17:57.080 --> 00:17:59.480
- Yeah!
- So good!

338
00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:04.520
Last day in the castle.
your last-ever breakfast here.

339
00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:06.680
By the end of today.
we are going to find out

340
00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:09.240
who's walking away
with the prize fund.

341
00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:15.920
and it currently stands at £76.750.

342
00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:20.760
But before that. you have
the mission of all missions.

343
00:18:20.760 --> 00:18:23.080
And I'm going to be honest.
it's going to be tough.

344
00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:25.800
I'm very pleased
I'm not on your boat.

345
00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:28.840
I'll see you at the mission.
and congratulations.

346
00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:32.880
- Thank you!
- Thank you. Claud!
- Oh. are we getting wet again?

347
00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:34.800
LAUGHTER

348
00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:40.200
This morning.
I need to plant seeds.

349
00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:44.040
Rachel is up against the ropes
after that Round Table last night.

350
00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:46.560
I cannot make myself
look more suspicious

351
00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:48.600
by not putting her name out there.

352
00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:56.960
I'm going to make a cup of tea.
Jade. and then go outside.

353
00:18:56.960 --> 00:18:58.600
if you want to come for a wee walk.

354
00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:10.360
- OK. we can...
- We need to go out and speak.

355
00:19:11.720 --> 00:19:14.640
But quickly.
before we get tagalongs.

356
00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:23.680
- What you saying. cuz?
- I wanted to
get you on your own.
- Yeah.

357
00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:25.960
I wanted to tell you something
very important.

358
00:19:25.960 --> 00:19:27.800
- Yeah.
- And this doesn't leave
this room.

359
00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:31.360
After last night's Round Table.

360
00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:33.400
Faraaz told me he thinks
he made a mistake.

361
00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:36.840
And he thinks my reaction told him
that it wasn't me.

362
00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:39.560
So all I've done is lean into that.

363
00:19:39.560 --> 00:19:43.480
I might be on the ropes. but
I'm not going down without a fight.

364
00:19:43.480 --> 00:19:46.440
What's one last lie between friends?

365
00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:49.840
I know about body language
and microexpressions

366
00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:53.560
and I have known who a Traitor was
from the very first night.

367
00:19:53.560 --> 00:19:58.000
and I have hid behind them
to try and get to the final.

368
00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.480
And when they turned on me
last night.

369
00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:02.680
I thought I might as well
spill my guts.

370
00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:05.120
So. it's Jade.

371
00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:07.880
I have known from the start.

372
00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:11.760
Her demeanour at the table
and her body language.

373
00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:14.160
she clenches here on this side.

374
00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:17.240
which I can see
every night she talks.

375
00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:20.440
- Oh. I see that. I see that.
- I don't trust those three.

376
00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:22.120
- Yeah.
- I do not trust those three.
- Yeah.

377
00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:25.000
If she gets into the final.
you've lost.

378
00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:28.160
I was literally thinking of
saying that. this morning.

379
00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:31.680
- it was Jade and Stephen for me.
- Yeah. I think so too.

380
00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:32.720
They've just been doing it...

381
00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:34.880
They've been inseparable
the past few days.

382
00:20:34.880 --> 00:20:38.040
I was going to vote Jade first
and then vote Stephen after.

383
00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:41.080
- Right. think... It's a number game.
- Yeah.
- If Jade goes...

384
00:20:41.080 --> 00:20:44.760
- Mm-hm.
- ..that leaves in one Traitor.
- Yeah.

385
00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:47.440
- And I would be more inclined
to go with Stephen.
- Yeah.

386
00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:50.000
With Rachel. I don't know
if she's someone I can trust.

387
00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:52.440
but she makes quite a lot of sense
with what she says.

388
00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:53.720
It is well-thought-out.

389
00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:56.480
You know after
the Round Table finished.

390
00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:58.000
I was the first to stand
and walk out. right?

391
00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:00.320
You know James.
how he went. "Tr-..."?

392
00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:03.840
- I jolted my chair back.
- I jumped up.
- I jumped out of the seat.

393
00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:06.480
The two of them next to me
did not flinch.

394
00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:08.560
- What?!
- I was out of my seat.
- Can I...?

395
00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:10.400
Can I share my post-cry clarity?

396
00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:12.880
- Cos...
- Yeah.
- ..it's fresh
in my mind. but I'm trusting

397
00:21:12.880 --> 00:21:14.720
- that you guys won't share it
with them.
- Mm-mm.

398
00:21:14.720 --> 00:21:17.120
Well. first and foremost. obviously.
I can't keep going over it

399
00:21:17.120 --> 00:21:19.240
in my head now. I made the mistake
of changing my vote

400
00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:22.360
because I was more convinced
by Rachel's final plea than James's.

401
00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:26.680
- Yeah.
- Before the Round Table. I felt
energy off her that was different.

402
00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:30.240
It's the first time I've seen Rachel
acting in a way that looked nervous.

403
00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:32.240
- Yeah.
- And she's such
a confident player.

404
00:21:32.240 --> 00:21:34.280
I'm almost certain it's Rachel.

405
00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:49.080
- I've told Faraaz about my suspicions
of Jade.
- Yeah.

406
00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:52.920
No.

407
00:21:56.920 --> 00:21:57.960
Mm-hm.

408
00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:02.040
Uh-huh.

409
00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:03.160
I know. I know. I know.

410
00:22:06.640 --> 00:22:07.680
Yeah. yeah. yeah.

411
00:22:15.840 --> 00:22:17.640
- After you!
- Thanks. mate.

412
00:22:17.640 --> 00:22:23.280
The prize fund currently stands
at £76.750.

413
00:22:23.280 --> 00:22:25.560
Today's final mission
is the last chance

414
00:22:25.560 --> 00:22:28.880
for the players to work together
to add to the pot.

415
00:22:31.560 --> 00:22:34.000
How do we feel about it being
the final day?

416
00:22:34.000 --> 00:22:37.280
It feels like the full experience
from mission one to now.

417
00:22:37.280 --> 00:22:38.520
You've done it all.

418
00:22:38.520 --> 00:22:40.240
We do really work well as a team.

419
00:22:40.240 --> 00:22:43.240
In the missions. yeah. we do.
At the Round Table. we don't.

420
00:22:43.240 --> 00:22:44.920
But at the missions. we do!

421
00:22:47.400 --> 00:22:49.400
Claudia always likes to go out
with a bang. doesn't she?

422
00:22:51.240 --> 00:22:53.720
- It's going to be like
Mission: Impossible.
- Yeah.

423
00:22:56.600 --> 00:22:58.080
Oh. Faraaz. it looks cold.

424
00:23:00.520 --> 00:23:02.920
- Oh. my goodness.
- Oh. there's Claudia.

425
00:23:02.920 --> 00:23:04.640
Oh. there she is!

426
00:23:06.920 --> 00:23:09.520
- Hi!
- Hi.

427
00:23:09.520 --> 00:23:13.320
I honestly can't believe that
I've made it to the final mission.

428
00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:15.800
It is just like
this surreal experience.

429
00:23:15.800 --> 00:23:17.480
Am I actually here?

430
00:23:17.480 --> 00:23:22.920
My final five.
welcome to your final mission.

431
00:23:22.920 --> 00:23:26.520
We've brought you into the heart
of the beautiful Highlands.

432
00:23:28.760 --> 00:23:34.200
On that stunning loch is £10.000.

433
00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:38.560
Pretty soon. you'll split into
two groups

434
00:23:38.560 --> 00:23:41.560
and get into those two speedboats.

435
00:23:41.560 --> 00:23:44.640
You have 45 minutes
to cross the loch.

436
00:23:44.640 --> 00:23:47.880
gathering the money.

437
00:23:47.880 --> 00:23:52.880
To help you find it. green flares
will signal the gold's location.

438
00:23:52.880 --> 00:23:57.480
but if the flare turns red
before you reach the location.

439
00:23:57.480 --> 00:24:02.920
I'm afraid it means you're too late.
You'll lose that gold forever.

440
00:24:02.920 --> 00:24:06.480
Once you have attempted
to collect all the gold.

441
00:24:06.480 --> 00:24:10.160
you just go to the end of the loch.
round that headland.

442
00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:12.720
and you bring it to me.

443
00:24:12.720 --> 00:24:17.840
And there. you will also
find your ride home.

444
00:24:17.840 --> 00:24:20.040
No!

445
00:24:20.040 --> 00:24:21.720
Oh. my God!

446
00:24:21.720 --> 00:24:23.680
SHOUTING

447
00:24:23.680 --> 00:24:26.040
SCREAMING

448
00:24:26.040 --> 00:24:27.960
I've got a helicopter
flying over my head.

449
00:24:27.960 --> 00:24:31.280
I've got boats on a loch.
thousands of pounds.

450
00:24:31.280 --> 00:24:33.880
The whole situation feels like
some sort of. like.

451
00:24:33.880 --> 00:24:36.200
hilarious fever dream.
And I love it.

452
00:24:37.920 --> 00:24:42.560
{\an8}Good luck.
Your 45 minutes starts...now!

453
00:24:42.560 --> 00:24:43.880
{\an8}HORN BLOWS

454
00:24:43.880 --> 00:24:46.160
{\an8}- OK. let's go. let's go. let's go.
- Go. go. go!

455
00:24:46.160 --> 00:24:48.040
{\an8}Go. go. go. go. go. go. go!

456
00:24:48.040 --> 00:24:50.480
What they don't know is
they're going to meet me

457
00:24:50.480 --> 00:24:53.160
at the top of an enormous dam.

458
00:24:55.480 --> 00:25:00.520
And it is a very long way down
to their ride home.

459
00:25:00.520 --> 00:25:03.280
This? This is just the starter.

460
00:25:03.280 --> 00:25:04.920
{\an8}That's it!

461
00:25:04.920 --> 00:25:07.600
{\an8}So I'm going to the middle. right?

462
00:25:07.600 --> 00:25:09.120
OK!

463
00:25:09.120 --> 00:25:10.840
LAUGHTER

464
00:25:10.840 --> 00:25:12.880
{\an8}- I'm going to go over there
somewhere.
- Over here?

465
00:25:12.880 --> 00:25:14.280
{\an8}- Yeah.
- Sorry about the...

466
00:25:12.880 --> 00:25:14.280
{\an8}LAUGHTER

467
00:25:14.280 --> 00:25:16.240
{\an8}I know. I know! I'm sorry!

468
00:25:17.440 --> 00:25:21.160
Around the loch
were different pontoons.

469
00:25:21.160 --> 00:25:25.320
We had to wait to see a flare
of green smoke.

470
00:25:26.480 --> 00:25:29.440
{\an8}- Green there!
- Go. go. go. go!
- Go. go. go. go!

471
00:25:29.440 --> 00:25:31.440
{\an8}Jade. we're going for
the green smoke now.

472
00:25:31.440 --> 00:25:32.760
{\an8}You guys get into the middle.

473
00:25:32.760 --> 00:25:35.600
And we then had to get over
to that pontoon...

474
00:25:35.600 --> 00:25:37.280
Right. keep going. keep going.

475
00:25:37.280 --> 00:25:41.360
..grab the money in time
or we got absolutely nothing.

476
00:25:41.360 --> 00:25:43.760
{\an8}- Got it. got it.
- That's two grand we've got.

477
00:25:43.760 --> 00:25:46.800
{\an8}They've got to the first pontoon.
They've retrieved the gold.

478
00:25:48.360 --> 00:25:50.840
{\an8}Oh. did they not get there?
No. look. yous go to that one.

479
00:25:50.840 --> 00:25:52.320
{\an8}We need to stay here.

480
00:25:52.320 --> 00:25:53.360
{\an8}We're on our way.

481
00:25:58.120 --> 00:26:00.760
{\an8}- There's green!
- Shit!

482
00:26:00.760 --> 00:26:03.080
{\an8}- Can you guys make that one?
- Yeah.
yeah. we're going to go for it.

483
00:26:03.080 --> 00:26:04.400
{\an8}We're going to go for it.

484
00:26:07.320 --> 00:26:09.560
If they don't want to leave
any money floating out there

485
00:26:09.560 --> 00:26:12.200
on the loch. I suggest
they move fast.

486
00:26:13.280 --> 00:26:15.440
{\an8}Why's our boat so slow?!

487
00:26:15.440 --> 00:26:17.640
{\an8}We're being taken by the waves.

488
00:26:17.640 --> 00:26:18.680
I'll do what I can.

489
00:26:20.400 --> 00:26:22.720
- Oh. it's red.
- Oh. what?

490
00:26:22.720 --> 00:26:24.600
We missed it. It's red.
Sorry. guys.

491
00:26:26.160 --> 00:26:30.240
{\an8}- Go. go. go. go. go. go!
- Keep going.
keep going. keep going. keep going!

492
00:26:34.680 --> 00:26:36.520
{\an8}- Well done.
- Go back. go back. go back!

493
00:26:38.440 --> 00:26:40.960
{\an8}It's there. One there. one there.
to the right. to the right.

494
00:26:40.960 --> 00:26:44.720
{\an8}Just something about racing it
across the loch with the wind.

495
00:26:44.720 --> 00:26:46.280
{\an8}We were so full of adrenaline
to make sure

496
00:26:46.280 --> 00:26:48.400
{\an8}that we could get to
the green flares on time.

497
00:26:48.400 --> 00:26:51.280
- OK. OK.
- You ready?
Yeah? You got it?

498
00:26:53.040 --> 00:26:55.720
{\an8}- Got it.
- Yes! Oh. yeah!

499
00:26:55.720 --> 00:26:59.960
{\an8}You've gone to all of the pontoons!
Come to me!

500
00:26:59.960 --> 00:27:03.840
{\an8}- Find me!
- Claudia. where are you?
- What. there?

501
00:27:03.840 --> 00:27:06.640
That's not Claudia. like. there.
is it?

502
00:27:06.640 --> 00:27:08.040
Hey!

503
00:27:08.040 --> 00:27:11.240
We see you!

504
00:27:13.080 --> 00:27:15.600
- Hang on! What?
- What is going on?

505
00:27:16.640 --> 00:27:18.760
- We're climbing that ladder?
- Yeah. the ladder.

506
00:27:18.760 --> 00:27:19.960
Shut up!

507
00:27:19.960 --> 00:27:22.840
{\an8}- Oh. my God!
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

508
00:27:24.360 --> 00:27:27.320
{\an8}Oh. my God! No!

509
00:27:24.360 --> 00:27:27.320
{\an8}LAUGHTER

510
00:27:27.320 --> 00:27:28.840
- Is that the ladder?!
- Yeah!

511
00:27:28.840 --> 00:27:30.080
Are you all right going first. Jade?

512
00:27:30.080 --> 00:27:33.680
{\an8}We had to climb a ladder up the dam.
which was so high.

513
00:27:33.680 --> 00:27:36.840
What?! It moves so much!

514
00:27:36.840 --> 00:27:38.680
Oh. my God.

515
00:27:38.680 --> 00:27:41.200
I guess the most important thing is.
don't look down.

516
00:27:41.200 --> 00:27:43.400
Jade! Yes!

517
00:27:43.400 --> 00:27:45.120
JADE SCREAMS

518
00:27:45.120 --> 00:27:48.000
The most uncomfortable part
is the wedgie that I have right now.

519
00:27:48.000 --> 00:27:49.960
It was so uncomfortable.

520
00:27:49.960 --> 00:27:54.600
the worst wedgie I've ever had
in my life!

521
00:27:54.600 --> 00:27:56.560
Oh. my God!

522
00:27:56.560 --> 00:27:58.160
What am I doing?!

523
00:27:58.160 --> 00:27:59.600
Let's go. Stephen!

524
00:27:59.600 --> 00:28:01.960
Oh. my God! Oh!

525
00:28:01.960 --> 00:28:04.920
Oh. my God. it's so high!

526
00:28:04.920 --> 00:28:06.400
Whoa!

527
00:28:06.400 --> 00:28:08.720
Oh... Oh. my legs are like jelly.

528
00:28:08.720 --> 00:28:10.160
Come on. Grandma.

529
00:28:10.160 --> 00:28:13.040
It's very. very different
when you have a genuine fear.

530
00:28:13.040 --> 00:28:14.400
I don't really like heights.

531
00:28:16.000 --> 00:28:20.080
{\an8}- Keep going. Rachel!
- I'm not afraid of heights.

532
00:28:20.080 --> 00:28:21.800
I can do this.

533
00:28:21.800 --> 00:28:23.880
I'm not afraid of heights.

534
00:28:23.880 --> 00:28:25.200
I didn't look down once.

535
00:28:25.200 --> 00:28:27.760
because if I had've looked down
once. it was game over.

536
00:28:29.240 --> 00:28:31.400
There's only five minutes left.
Come on!

537
00:28:33.120 --> 00:28:35.720
They're almost there. almost there.
almost there.

538
00:28:39.800 --> 00:28:43.360
- Yes!
- Come on. Rachel!
- Come on!

539
00:28:48.040 --> 00:28:51.200
Yes. Rachel!
Come on!

540
00:28:52.160 --> 00:28:53.760
{\an8}I'm not the best with heights.

541
00:28:53.760 --> 00:28:55.880
{\an8}And my legs are starting to go
a bit wobbly.

542
00:28:55.880 --> 00:28:59.280
There was a lot of nervous energy
going through me then.

543
00:28:59.280 --> 00:29:03.360
Well done. We need Faraaz.
Otherwise. this money is not banked.

544
00:29:03.360 --> 00:29:05.360
{\an8}Come on. Faraaz!

545
00:29:03.360 --> 00:29:05.360
{\an8}SHOUTING

546
00:29:05.360 --> 00:29:08.680
{\an8}- Faraaz. come on. Come on!
- Quick. quick. quick!

547
00:29:08.680 --> 00:29:11.320
{\an8}- Hurry up!
- Come on. Faraaz!

548
00:29:11.320 --> 00:29:14.960
THEY SHOUT

549
00:29:14.960 --> 00:29:17.160
THEY CHEER

550
00:29:19.240 --> 00:29:20.880
Well done!

551
00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:25.560
Players. you did that
so brilliantly.

552
00:29:25.560 --> 00:29:30.760
And you have added £9.000
to the prize fund.

553
00:29:30.760 --> 00:29:31.840
Well done!

554
00:29:33.120 --> 00:29:35.000
Let me just tell you this -

555
00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:36.720
I'm going to give you the chance

556
00:29:36.720 --> 00:29:40.440
to add another £10.000
to the prize fund.

557
00:29:41.680 --> 00:29:46.560
All you have to do is get
to your ride. that helicopter.

558
00:29:46.560 --> 00:29:48.200
in five minutes.

559
00:29:49.560 --> 00:29:50.840
That's all you have to do.

560
00:29:52.320 --> 00:29:54.520
Here's the tricky bit.

561
00:29:54.520 --> 00:29:57.840
The only way to get
to that helicopter

562
00:29:57.840 --> 00:30:00.720
- is to step off...
- Oh!
- ..this edge.

563
00:30:07.720 --> 00:30:10.800
You will be running down the dam.
facing forward.

564
00:30:10.800 --> 00:30:13.800
No! No. No.

565
00:30:16.400 --> 00:30:19.360
- Are you serious?
- I'm deadly serious. Rachel.

566
00:30:23.320 --> 00:30:25.120
OK. enormous luck.

567
00:30:26.120 --> 00:30:28.080
Go get yourselves ready.

568
00:30:28.080 --> 00:30:30.800
My knees started to go.
and I thought.

569
00:30:30.800 --> 00:30:33.520
"I'm either going to vomit.
I'm going to faint.

570
00:30:33.520 --> 00:30:35.520
"or I'm just going to refuse
to do this."

571
00:30:37.840 --> 00:30:40.840
You all right?
You're not all right. OK.

572
00:30:40.840 --> 00:30:43.920
So you three are on this ledge.

573
00:30:43.920 --> 00:30:46.200
The other two are on
a different ledge.

574
00:30:47.400 --> 00:30:49.320
- This is ridiculous.
- This is insane.

575
00:30:50.920 --> 00:30:54.600
I honestly thought my knees
were going to go from under me.

576
00:30:57.160 --> 00:30:58.200
Don't look.

577
00:31:02.520 --> 00:31:04.520
Everything starts to
come into focus.

578
00:31:04.520 --> 00:31:08.960
and you start seeing
how high up you are.

579
00:31:08.960 --> 00:31:12.000
For the team and to bank that money.

580
00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:13.120
I knew I had to do it.

581
00:31:15.480 --> 00:31:17.720
Oh. this feels so weird!

582
00:31:17.720 --> 00:31:20.200
No. no. no. This is too much.

583
00:31:20.200 --> 00:31:21.600
This is too high.

584
00:31:21.600 --> 00:31:23.000
- Good luck. Jade.
- Yeah!

585
00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:24.600
HE LAUGHS

586
00:31:24.600 --> 00:31:27.680
Players. your five minutes starts.

587
00:31:27.680 --> 00:31:31.160
Three. two. one...

588
00:31:31.160 --> 00:31:33.440
HORN BLOWS

589
00:31:33.440 --> 00:31:34.760
{\an8}Oh. geez!

590
00:31:36.320 --> 00:31:37.360
{\an8}Whoa!

591
00:31:40.320 --> 00:31:43.040
- Whoa!
- Oh. my God!

592
00:31:43.040 --> 00:31:45.480
It petrified me.

593
00:31:45.480 --> 00:31:46.600
Oh. my God!

594
00:31:46.600 --> 00:31:49.720
But at that point.
there's only one way to go.

595
00:31:49.720 --> 00:31:51.960
I had to go down.

596
00:31:51.960 --> 00:31:54.840
- That's it. Rach!
- Whee!

597
00:31:54.840 --> 00:31:57.480
- Wait. Jade. you're doing it better
than me.
- Woo!

598
00:31:59.080 --> 00:32:01.120
Faraaz. you're OK.
You can do it.

599
00:32:03.280 --> 00:32:05.400
- Bloody hell!
- Faraaz. well done.

600
00:32:09.840 --> 00:32:12.240
{\an8}Oh...

601
00:32:09.840 --> 00:32:12.240
{\an8}SHE SCREAMS

602
00:32:12.240 --> 00:32:14.200
{\an8}HE GROANS

603
00:32:16.160 --> 00:32:18.640
{\an8}You're doing good. Rachel!

604
00:32:16.160 --> 00:32:18.640
{\an8}THEY LAUGH

605
00:32:21.440 --> 00:32:23.280
{\an8}JACK LAUGHS

606
00:32:23.280 --> 00:32:25.680
Jade. how insane is this?

607
00:32:23.280 --> 00:32:25.680
JADE LAUGHS

608
00:32:27.640 --> 00:32:30.520
I just saw Rachel sprint
in front of me.

609
00:32:30.520 --> 00:32:33.080
I mean. she was a machine.

610
00:32:34.680 --> 00:32:37.600
Jade's at the bottom.
Jack is at the bottom!

611
00:32:37.600 --> 00:32:39.240
{\an8}What? What is going on here?

612
00:32:39.240 --> 00:32:41.480
You have got this!
You're amazing!

613
00:32:42.640 --> 00:32:44.040
Done it!

614
00:32:44.040 --> 00:32:46.160
- Well done. Rachel!
- Oh!

615
00:32:48.280 --> 00:32:50.560
{\an8}Let's go. Stephen!

616
00:32:51.720 --> 00:32:54.760
{\an8}Yes! Well done!

617
00:32:54.760 --> 00:32:58.800
- Come on. Faraaz!
- Yeah. yeah!
Well done!

618
00:32:59.880 --> 00:33:01.640
- Guys. we've got to get to
the helicopter. Come on!
- Hug later!

619
00:33:01.640 --> 00:33:03.720
Hug later! Helicopter first.
hug later.

620
00:33:06.000 --> 00:33:07.680
{\an8}- Here.
- Go on!

621
00:33:12.080 --> 00:33:15.320
- They did it!
- That was unbelievable.

622
00:33:17.360 --> 00:33:19.960
And I'm really. really proud
that I pushed myself to do it.

623
00:33:19.960 --> 00:33:23.280
Oh...

624
00:33:19.960 --> 00:33:23.280
THEY LAUGH

625
00:33:23.280 --> 00:33:25.520
Come on! Yes!

626
00:33:26.720 --> 00:33:28.600
{\an8} Bye. Claudia!

627
00:33:29.800 --> 00:33:33.520
Oh. my gosh!

628
00:33:33.520 --> 00:33:34.880
Whew!

629
00:33:38.560 --> 00:33:40.520
SHE LAUGHS

630
00:33:40.520 --> 00:33:45.040
# Blue sky smiling at me... #

631
00:33:45.040 --> 00:33:47.400
- Wow. look at this!
- Wow!

632
00:33:47.400 --> 00:33:48.960
- This is ridiculous!
- Unreal!

633
00:33:48.960 --> 00:33:53.000
I just had
the most amazing time today.

634
00:33:53.000 --> 00:33:54.760
and I don't want to taint it
thinking about

635
00:33:54.760 --> 00:33:57.640
the horrible Round Table
that's coming up tonight!

636
00:33:57.640 --> 00:33:59.040
HE GROANS

637
00:33:59.040 --> 00:34:01.200
THEY SCREAM. LAUGH

638
00:34:03.200 --> 00:34:05.560
Oh. my God!

639
00:34:05.560 --> 00:34:07.760
Is this not the best mission ever?

640
00:34:07.760 --> 00:34:12.040
- Oh. yeah.
- Yeah.
Guys. 19 grand.

641
00:34:12.040 --> 00:34:15.240
- What's our pot. like 95K
or something?
- Yeah.

642
00:34:15.240 --> 00:34:16.840
It's a lot of dough.

643
00:34:16.840 --> 00:34:19.560
I don't think money is
a motivating factor for Stephen.

644
00:34:19.560 --> 00:34:23.600
but did that huge amount
that we won today make him think.

645
00:34:23.600 --> 00:34:25.240
"I can do all of this on my own"?

646
00:34:25.240 --> 00:34:27.000
The castle!

647
00:34:27.000 --> 00:34:29.920
- Oh. my goodness me!
- That's stunning.

648
00:34:29.920 --> 00:34:33.400
I know exactly what I need to do
tonight to win this game.

649
00:34:33.400 --> 00:34:35.440
Stephen knows what he needs to do.

650
00:34:35.440 --> 00:34:37.600
It's whether or not
he can hold his nerve

651
00:34:37.600 --> 00:34:39.480
and that money
doesn't turn his head.

652
00:34:45.680 --> 00:34:47.600
We just came out
of a helicopter!

653
00:34:47.600 --> 00:34:49.720
Oh. my God!

654
00:34:49.720 --> 00:34:52.200
I just... I can't stop thinking
about that moment

655
00:34:52.200 --> 00:34:56.480
when you and I looked at each other
and we both had one hand on the bar.

656
00:34:56.480 --> 00:34:58.800
"Come on. you go first!"

657
00:34:56.480 --> 00:34:58.800
THEY LAUGH

658
00:34:58.800 --> 00:35:00.120
Oh. that was nuts. wasn't it?

659
00:35:00.120 --> 00:35:03.760
- My legs are still like jelly.
- Yeah. mine too!

660
00:35:03.760 --> 00:35:05.440
- But what an experience. though.
- Oh!

661
00:35:08.480 --> 00:35:11.120
How are you feeling
coming into the...? I don't know.

662
00:35:11.120 --> 00:35:12.280
I think I know who I'm going to...

663
00:35:12.280 --> 00:35:14.440
..yeah. I'm going to go for
on the Round Table.

664
00:35:14.440 --> 00:35:18.120
There's a common theme
where Traitors try and almost like

665
00:35:18.120 --> 00:35:20.160
guilt-trip people before they go.

666
00:35:28.240 --> 00:35:29.840
Yeah. she got very defensive
about it.

667
00:35:29.840 --> 00:35:32.040
And it worked for me
cos I changed my mind.

668
00:35:32.040 --> 00:35:34.640
You know. Faraaz hasn't voted
for a single Traitor.

669
00:35:36.800 --> 00:35:39.080
- He hasn't voted for Hugo.
- Not for Fiona either.

670
00:35:39.080 --> 00:35:40.120
He didn't vote for Fiona.

671
00:35:41.200 --> 00:35:42.280
I didn't notice that.

672
00:35:44.080 --> 00:35:45.960
Did he vote for Rachel
at the last one?

673
00:35:45.960 --> 00:35:48.080
Yeah. but then
after the Round Table.

674
00:35:48.080 --> 00:35:51.400
he was like. "Oh. yeah.
I'm really sorry I voted for you."

675
00:35:51.400 --> 00:35:53.120
- I was like...
- Yeah. he told me he
changed his mind...

676
00:35:53.120 --> 00:35:54.480
.."Are you backing down?"

677
00:35:54.480 --> 00:35:56.760
- Mmm.
- Like. you've come after me
with such conviction.

678
00:35:56.760 --> 00:35:58.400
you went after Sam
with such conviction.

679
00:35:58.400 --> 00:36:00.720
- Like...
- Why has he suddenly changed
his mind?
- Do you know what I mean?

680
00:36:00.720 --> 00:36:04.760
I think Faraaz being able
to coast through the game.

681
00:36:04.760 --> 00:36:07.680
not voted out a Traitor.
and to be able to stay so calm

682
00:36:07.680 --> 00:36:10.440
and collected at the Round Table.
I think it's because you know

683
00:36:10.440 --> 00:36:12.120
that you've got the majority
of the power.

684
00:36:12.120 --> 00:36:13.920
and I think that's
because he's a Traitor.

685
00:36:15.760 --> 00:36:17.680
Just to go into the library
and have a wee read.

686
00:36:20.160 --> 00:36:22.680
Last night was just so brutal.

687
00:36:22.680 --> 00:36:27.000
Well. it mightn't mean an awful lot.
but I really appreciated your vote.

688
00:36:27.000 --> 00:36:29.960
And going into tonight.
I've already said it to Faraaz -

689
00:36:29.960 --> 00:36:32.240
I'm not saying who I'm voting for.

690
00:36:32.240 --> 00:36:34.800
I'm... For the first time.
I'm going to hold my cards

691
00:36:34.800 --> 00:36:36.320
- close to my chest...
- That's fair enough. yeah.

692
00:36:36.320 --> 00:36:39.240
..because I felt so
vulnerable last night.

693
00:36:39.240 --> 00:36:41.080
- Can I join in on...?
- Yeah.
- You can. of course.

694
00:36:41.080 --> 00:36:42.920
- You all right. man?
- Yeah. sport.
Y'all right?
- Yeah.

695
00:36:46.520 --> 00:36:49.120
- Am I all right to talk to Jack
for a bit? Is that all right?
- Sure.

696
00:36:49.120 --> 00:36:52.560
I'm leaning really. really heavily
on Faraaz to get Jade out.

697
00:36:52.560 --> 00:36:56.320
so any conversation in private
just makes me feel nervous.

698
00:36:56.320 --> 00:36:59.480
This doesn't leave this room. right?
It's a game of numbers.

699
00:36:59.480 --> 00:37:02.400
We need to vote Jade first. then
I'll go with you and vote Rachel

700
00:37:02.400 --> 00:37:05.040
and then we vote Stephen
and we win it together.

701
00:37:05.040 --> 00:37:07.280
Cos I just want to be stood
there with you at the end.

702
00:37:07.280 --> 00:37:11.520
I don't think Rachel is a Traitor.
but I'm not 100% convinced with it.

703
00:37:11.520 --> 00:37:13.680
I'm 99. and 99 is not enough.

704
00:37:13.680 --> 00:37:17.520
So the only person I do trust
100% in this game is Jack.

705
00:37:19.760 --> 00:37:21.920
See. my plan was that I was
going to vote Rachel first.

706
00:37:21.920 --> 00:37:25.400
No. vote... I'm telling you.
because Rachel's voting Jade first.

707
00:37:25.400 --> 00:37:26.720
How do you know
who she's going to vote for?

708
00:37:26.720 --> 00:37:28.560
She told me in confidence
because she trusts me.

709
00:37:28.560 --> 00:37:30.000
So she's just lied to my face.

710
00:37:32.240 --> 00:37:36.240
I'm convinced. 100%
convinced it is Rachel.

711
00:37:36.240 --> 00:37:39.120
That aside. I don't know
who I can really trust fully.

712
00:37:41.840 --> 00:37:43.880
Me and Jack were just
talking about Rachel

713
00:37:43.880 --> 00:37:45.520
at last night's round table.

714
00:37:45.520 --> 00:37:47.520
She was. like. basically
guilt-tripping.

715
00:37:47.520 --> 00:37:50.920
The way that James
presented himself at the end

716
00:37:50.920 --> 00:37:53.320
was just someone that had
absolutely nothing to prove.

717
00:37:53.320 --> 00:37:57.640
And then I'm wondering if.
because her defence was

718
00:37:57.640 --> 00:38:01.800
so articulate and thought out.
is that actually what it was. like.

719
00:38:01.800 --> 00:38:03.800
- thought out...?
- And rehearsed.

720
00:38:05.440 --> 00:38:07.600
I think. like. that's something
that has been playing on my mind

721
00:38:07.600 --> 00:38:11.760
a lot. and round the table
tonight I just don't know

722
00:38:11.760 --> 00:38:15.160
if I can carry on with that
still in the game.

